---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What openslm.ai collects, what it doesn't, and how to change your mind."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>

  <section class="hero hero--page">
    <div class="container-page hero__inner">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">What this site<br />collects.</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">
        OpenSLM.ai is a documents site. The default state is no analytics, no
        cookies, no profiling. Anything beyond that requires you to opt in,
        and you can change your mind at any time on this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-mark" aria-hidden="true">§</div>

  <section class="tail-section">
    <div class="container-page tail-section__inner privacy-prose">

      <h2>What runs by default</h2>
      <p>
        On a fresh visit, no analytics tag loads. Your browser fetches the page,
        the static assets, and the fonts. There is no third-party tracking, no
        advertising network, no cookie. Server access logs are kept by the host
        (GitHub Pages) and are not used by this site.
      </p>

      <h2>What runs only if you accept</h2>
      <p>
        If you click <strong>Accept</strong> on the consent banner, this site
        loads <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/clarity/" rel="external noopener">Microsoft Clarity</a>.
        Clarity is an anonymous usage analytics tool from Microsoft. It sets
        cookies and records:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Pages you view and the order you view them in.</li>
        <li>Anonymized session replays of how you move and click on the page.</li>
        <li>Aggregated heatmaps of where visitors scroll and click.</li>
        <li>Browser, operating system, and approximate region (country / city).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Clarity does <em>not</em> collect form contents on this site (we don't
        have form inputs), does not build advertising profiles, and does not
        sell data to third parties. Microsoft documents its data use at the
        link above. Data sent to Clarity is processed by Microsoft on
        infrastructure outside this project's control.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we ask</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a public document. Knowing which sections people read, where
        they get stuck, and which links never get followed helps us make the
        accord clearer over time. None of that requires identifying you. The
        consent prompt exists because Clarity uses cookies, and cookies require
        consent under the laws this site reads as binding (UK PECR, EU GDPR,
        California CPRA, and equivalents).
      </p>

      <h2>Your choice, right now</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your decision at any time. The button below applies
        immediately on this device and persists across visits.
      </p>

      <div class="privacy-actions" data-consent-controls>
        <p class="privacy-status" data-consent-status>Loading current setting…</p>
        <div class="privacy-buttons">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" data-consent-set="granted">Accept analytics</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-consent-set="declined">Decline analytics</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-consent-set="reset">Reset to ask again</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What this site never does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising. No retargeting. No ad networks.</li>
        <li>No login. No accounts. No identity tied to your reading.</li>
        <li>No selling, sharing, or licensing data to third parties beyond what is technically necessary to deliver the page (the host) or what you explicitly allowed (Clarity).</li>
        <li>No fingerprinting or device-graph linking initiated by this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, concerns, or rights requests:
        <a href="mailto:hello@openslm.ai">hello@openslm.ai</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="privacy-meta">
        This page is part of the openslm.ai source repository
        (<a href="https://github.com/openslm-ai/website">github.com/openslm-ai/website</a>),
        released under CC0 1.0 alongside the rest of the site. If our practice
        diverges from what is written here, that is a bug — file an issue.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var KEY = 'analytics-consent';
      var statusEl = document.querySelector('[data-consent-status]');
      var btns = document.querySelectorAll('[data-consent-set]');
      if (!statusEl || !btns.length) return;

      function read() {
        try { return localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (_) { return null; }
      }

      function reflect() {
        var v = read();
        if (v === 'granted') {
          statusEl.textContent = 'Current setting on this device: analytics enabled.';
        } else if (v === 'declined') {
          statusEl.textContent = 'Current setting on this device: analytics declined.';
        } else {
          statusEl.textContent = 'Current setting on this device: not yet decided. The banner will ask on your next page load.';
        }
      }

      reflect();

      btns.forEach(function (btn) {
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var v = btn.getAttribute('data-consent-set');
          try {
            if (v === 'reset') localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
            else localStorage.setItem(KEY, v);
          } catch (_) {}
          // For an immediate effect (loading or unloading Clarity) the page must
          // reload — Clarity has no documented in-page tear-down.
          location.reload();
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-prose {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  .privacy-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose p,
  .privacy-prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .privacy-actions {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .privacy-status {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .privacy-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .privacy-meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
